	(text "Values shown are the 22 A arm, waist, aux channel. Leg channels (DNP in rev A) change: Q502 fitted; RS501 1 mOhm (48.5-61.5 A) or 1.5 mOhm (32-41 A), no 1.2 mOhm part exists;\nRPWR 23.7k at 1 mOhm, 30.1k at 1.2 mOhm; INA228 SHUNT_CAL rescaled; fuse needs another format (997 MINI stops at 30 A).\nEnable: PORT_EN high (3V3, 100k down) turns Q3 on, Q2 off, UVLO released. Supervisor dead: Q2 on, UVLO low, port off. Latch reset: drop PORT_EN, wait 148 ms, raise it.\nILIM 19.4-24.6 A, breaker 32-52 A, fault timer 2.8-9.0 ms, UVLO on 32.0 V off 28.0 V, OVLO off 60.3 V. Starts on dV/dt: 47 nF covers 3.6 mF of drive capacitance.\nGND2: bus reference ties to the port return here. Galvanic isolation then separates LP logic ground from motor return; it does not block a CAN-to-VBUS fault, ISOW1044 survives that at +/-58 V.\nSMAJ58CA for sustained 54 V survival (NUP2105L VBR 26-32 V fails). Its clamp is above the ISOW1044 58 V limit and its capacitance is unchecked: scope on the bus."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60d1902e-e115-5e79-88ed-6caae7778a21")
	)
